<title>UK: Doughty Hanson poised to make new acquisition-paper.</title>
<headline>Doughty Hanson poised to make new acquisition-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private fund manager Doughty Hanson &amp; Co, fresh from taking over Swiss sanitary systems firm Geberit, is due to complete another large acquisition in the next few weeks, the Financial Times said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The paper said the firm, with a majority stake in the merged metal packaging businesses of Germany's Viag AG and France's Pechiney, has emerged as a significant player among venture capitalists groups in London.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
